after pass 4: 2 6 3 7 9 9 11 12
after pass 5: 2 3 6 7 9 9 11 12
after pass 6: 2 3 6 7 9 9 11 12
no exchanges -> sorted` },
        { type: "h3", text: "Cost" },
        { type: "p", text: "The slide’s implementation performs `(n−1) + (n−2) + … + 1 = n(n−1)/2` comparisons in the worst case, and the same bound on swaps in the worst case, for O(n²) overall. The early-exit flag shown above is the optimization described on slide 24: the algorithm does not know the list is sorted until it completes a pass with no exchanges. With the flag, a sorted input needs one pass and n−1 comparisons, so the best case becomes O(n)." },
